from pathlib import Path
import json,html
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;scores=json.loads((r/'scores.json').read_text());raw=json.loads((r/'normalized-results.json').read_text())
head='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Skanda | Labeled case review</title><style>body{background:#101216;color:#edf0f3;font:17px/1.6 system-ui;margin:0}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px}h1{font-size:44px;line-height:1.1;max-width:800px}p{max-width:850px;color:#bfc6ce}a{color:#83cfbf}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #333}th{color:#abb2ba}h2{margin-top:60px;font-size:30px}img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin-top:20px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#83cfbf;padding:12px 0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font:14px/1.5 monospace;color:#bbc3ce}section{margin:36px 0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #30343a}.note{padding:20px;border-left:2px solid #ffb578}nav{display:flex;gap:28px;margin:28px 0}@media(max-width:700px){h1{font-size:32px}table{font-size:12px}td,th{padding:8px 3px}}</style><main><h1>Detection and localization tell different stories.</h1><p>Actual tests in the existing Skanda application, 2 November 2026. One labeled CT volume and one labeled MRI volume; four selected axial slices per case. Model: skanda-grounding-q3-mixed.</p><nav><a href="#ct">CT results</a><a href="#mri">MRI results</a><a href="provenance.json">Sources and method</a><a href="app-results.json">Saved application outputs</a></nav><p class="note">This is a targeted demonstration on public training cases, not whole-volume validation or an independent clinical benchmark. Unknown training-set overlap. Reference-negative means no annotated target on that slice, not proof of a healthy scan.</p>'''
parts=[head]
for mod,title in [('ct','Liver CT / MSD liver_0'),('mri','Brain MRI / BraTS-GLI-00000-000')]:
 parts.append(f'<h2 id="{mod}">{title}</h2><table><tr><th>Axial slice</th><th>Reference target</th><th>Model lesion</th><th>Box-mask IoU</th><th>App flagged</th></tr>')
 for x in [x for x in scores if x['modality']==mod]:
  iou='No box' if x['boxToReferenceMaskIoU'] is None else f"{x['boxToReferenceMaskIoU']:.3f}"
  parts.append(f'<tr><td>{x["slice"]}</td><td>{"Present" if x["referencePositive"] else "Absent"}</td><td>{"Reported" if x["reportedAbnormal"] else "Not reported"}</td><td>{iou}</td><td>{"Yes" if x["appFlagged"] else "No"}</td></tr>')
 parts.append('</table><p>IoU compares the union of raw candidate boxes against the reference mask: intersection / union. It is not a segmentation Dice score or overall diagnostic accuracy. The app may withhold a raw box after its consistency checks.</p>')
 for x in [x for x in scores if x['modality']==mod]:
  record=next(y for y in raw if y['modality']==mod and y['slice']==x['slice'])
  parts.append(f'<section><h3>Axial {x["slice"]}</h3><p>{html.escape(x["impression"] or "No readable result")}</p><img src="{mod}-{x["slice"]}-comparison.png" alt="Original slice next to reference contour and raw model box"><details><summary>Actual app screenshot and output</summary><img src="{mod}-{x["slice"]}-app.png" alt="Application result"><pre>{html.escape(record["ui"])}</pre><pre>{html.escape(record["analysis"].get("rawText", ""))}</pre></details></section>')
parts.append('''<h2>Verification and limits</h2><p>Native voxel values, dimensions and image/mask affine were checked before lossless integer NRRD conversion. No reference masks were provided to the model. The selection manifest was fixed before inference. The final run verified request and response slice labels for all eight cases.</p><p>An exploratory pass contained one incorrect MRI slice request and incomplete raw-response capture. It is retained in first-pass-results.json and excluded from the final scores. All eight cases were repeated with identity assertions; model output varied between runs.</p><p>CT: labels 2 (liver tumor). MRI: union of labels 1, 2, 3, including tumor-associated edema. These annotation scopes differ. MRI is a single T1 post-contrast sequence; no ADC image was supplied, even where a response claimed an ADC value.</p><p>Source data: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/MedOtter/msd-liver">MSD Liver mirror</a> (declared CC-BY-SA-4.0); <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/MedOtter/brats2023-gli-dataset">BraTS 2023 GLI mirror</a> (declared CC-BY-4.0). Original projects: <a href="https://medicaldecathlon.com/">Medical Segmentation Decathlon</a>, <a href="https://www.synapse.org/Synapse:syn51156910/wiki/622351">BraTS 2023</a>. Full paths, hashes and label definitions are in provenance.json and manifest.json.</p></main>''')
(r/'review.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
